so  hello  the coronavirus continues to spread  rapidly  across europe we need a safe and  effective vaccine to end this pandemic  a few days after our contract with  biontech  and pfizer i'm happy to announce a new  agreement  tomorrow we will authorize a new  contract to secure  another covet 19 vaccines vaccine for  europeans  this contract allows us to buy up to  405 million doses  of a vaccine produced by the european  company curvac  earlier this year we have provided  funding to kurovac together with the  european investment bank  we did that to support the development  of these vaccines and now  progress is tangible if the vaccine has  proven  safe and effective against covet 19  every member state will receive the  vaccine  at the same time on a pro-rata basis  and under the same conditions this  is the fifth contract with the  pharmaceutical company  for our covet 19 vaccine portfolio  and we are working on a sixth one  with moderna we have already concluded  exploratory talks with moderna  we hope to finalize the contract soon  we do not know at this stage which  vaccine will end up being  safe and effective the european  medicines agency  emma will authorize them only after a  robust  assessment and this is why we need to  have a broad  portfolio of vaccines based on very  different technologies  in parallel we are working with covax  to provide access to vaccines for low  and middle income countries  thus we want to ensure that all have  access rapidly to safe and effective  vaccines thank you very much  [Music]  you

